.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt CUT 1
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm cut
.Nd select byte, character or field ranges from lines
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl b Ar list | Fl c Ar list | Fl f Ar list
.Op Fl d Ar delimiter
.Op Fl s
.Op Fl Fl complement
.Op Fl Fl output-delimiter Ar text
.Op Fl z
.Op Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Select one range mode:
.Fl b
for bytes,
.Fl c
for characters, or
.Fl f
for fields.
A list contains one-based positions and inclusive ranges separated by
commas: N, N-M, N-, or -M.
The selected pieces remain in input order; list order does not reorder them.
.Pp
Fields are tab-separated by default.
.Fl d Ar delimiter
changes the single-character field separator.
Lines without a field delimiter are passed through unless
.Fl s
suppresses them.
.Fl Fl complement
inverts the selection;
.Fl Fl output-delimiter Ar text
changes the separator between selected output pieces.
.Fl z
uses NUL in place of newline.
.Pp
Read named files in order, or standard input when no files are named;
.Ql -
explicitly selects standard input.
Write selections to standard output without modifying the inputs.
This is delimiter selection, not a quoted CSV parser.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on successful processing; nonzero for invalid selection/options,
unreadable input or output failure. Diagnostics use standard error.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
cut -d : -f 1,6 /etc/passwd.txt
.Ed
.Sh ABSD PROFILE
This is the unmodified uutils 0.12.0 utility pinned by the platform build.
The reference describes selected source-supported options; use
.Fl Fl help
for the complete upstream interface.
File access uses the process's ABSD filesystem view, output uses its
inherited stream, and the command acquires no additional authority.
There are no native Unix processes, signals or permission bits underneath
this port.
The command matrix exercises the example forms below; other options
listed here are source-checked, not separately guest-qualified.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cat 1 ,
.Xr wc 1 ,
.Xr filesystem 7
